# .env.example — pointer file, not a runtime template.
#
# This repository is documentation only; it does not read any .env file.
# The real variables live in the backend repository (backendTS):
#   - root .env.example                         shared values (JWT_SECRET, database passwords,
#                                               RabbitMQ, CORS, email, Google/Facebook)
#   - services/<service>/.env.example           values of each service: iam-service,
#                                               recognition-service, lexicon-service,
#                                               analytics-service, profile-service, api-gateway
#
# Each file's header explains how it is loaded (docker compose or local dev).
#
# JWT_SECRET
#   - Required. Minimum 32 characters (services refuse to start without it).
#   - Algorithm: HS256 (symmetric). iam-service signs the tokens; the other services verify them,
#     so the same value must be used in every service.
#   - Generate a local value with: openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Never commit real .env files or secret values. Production secrets go in the vault.

JWT_SECRET=
